.TH BABYSIT.CONF 5 "2026-11-15" "babysit" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
babysit.conf \- configuration for babysitd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/babysit/babysit.conf
.br
.I $HOME/.config/babysit/babysit.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
Settings for
.BR babysitd (8).
.BR babysit (1)
reads it too, for
.B timezone
only.
Each line is
.IR key " = " value .
Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored.
Unknown keys and bad values are reported and skipped.
.TP
.B timezone
.B local
or
.BR utc :
the clock by which
.BR babysit (1)
dates its instance identifiers and log directories, and by which
.BR babysitd (8)
decides which days and hours are over.
Change it to
.B utc
when
.B babysit
is used with automation.
Local time repeats an hour wherever clocks are set back in autumn, and for
that hour
.B babysit
finds records dated later than now and refuses to start (exit status 75)
until they are packed; UTC never does that.
Do not change the setting while there are unpacked logs: the same thing
happens for as many hours as the two clocks differ.
Default:
.BR local .
.TP
.B max_age_days
Delete archived logs and finished logs older than this many days.
0 keeps them forever.
Default: 30.
.TP
.B compact_at_disk_percent
When the filesystem holding the logs is at least this full, in percent,
also pack the finished hours of days that are not over yet, so that the
logs written so far are compressed.
0 disables.
Default: 90.
.TP
.B delete_at_disk_percent
When that filesystem is at least this full, in percent, delete packed logs
(archives of past days and packed hours),
oldest first, until it is not or none are left.
Live log directories are never deleted.
This is the only setting that removes logs before they reach
.BR max_age_days .
If the disk is full of other files it will delete every packed log without
bringing usage under the limit, so it is disabled unless set.
It is best set above
.BR compact_at_disk_percent ,
so that compression is tried first.
0 disables.
Default: 0.
.TP
.B check_interval
How often the service wakes up to do its housekeeping when nothing asks for
it sooner: a number with an
.BR s ,
.BR m ,
.B h
or
.B d
suffix (seconds if there is none).
.BR babysit (1)
wakes the service itself when it needs something packed before it can
start, so this can stay long.
Default: 6h.
.PP
Command-line options of
.B babysitd
override this file.
The file is read once, when the service starts.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
timezone = utc
max_age_days = 14
compact_at_disk_percent = 80
delete_at_disk_percent = 95
check_interval = 12h
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR babysitd (8),
.BR babysit (1)
